  "caveats": [
   "ECI holds occupational and industry composition constant by design. That is the right control for a scarcity question, but it means a shift toward more skilled workers within a trade does not register as wage pressure.",
   "The construction industry cut blends licensed journeymen with general labourers, so it may understate scarcity in the licensed subset. The construction-and-extraction occupational cut is the sharper read and tells the same story.",
   "Anchored to 2019Q4 to strip the pandemic wage distortion out of the base."
  ],
